=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A thorough inspection of all devices in the ospf_enterprise_static topology found no fault. The helpdesk ticket describes intermittent connectivity with "core links bouncing," but no such condition exists in the live lab. Every OSPF adjacency across all six FRR devices (router_core_1, router_core_2, router_core_3, switch_dist_1_1, switch_dist_2_1, switch_server_access) is stable in Full state with exactly 6 state changes per neighbor — precisely the normal Down→Init→2-Way→ExStart→Exchange→Loading→Full progression that occurred once during initial startup approximately 7 minutes ago. No state change has occurred since then. The FRR logs on every device contain only the startup configuration-load entries and the initial OSPF negotiation handshake; there are no adjacency-down events, no restarts, and no log entries indicating any subsequent disruption. All core interfaces (router_core_1/2/3 eth0, eth1, eth2) report zero errors, zero drops, and zero carrier events in their counters. End-to-end connectivity tests from host_1_1_1_1 and host_2_1_1_1 to the server farm (10.200.0.0/24) yield 0% packet loss with sub-3 ms latency. Routing tables on all devices are correctly populated via OSPF with the expected inter-area and intra-area routes. No cron jobs, background scripts, or unusual processes were found on any device. The network is fully healthy. The complaint of bouncing likely arose from the brief OSPF convergence period at lab startup (normal, lasting under 60 seconds), which may have been misinterpreted as a recurring fault. No corrective action is required.
=== END ===